  "code_hypotheses": {
    "primary": "Runtime.emitNative attempts QueueBytes reservation for complete retained response before each event; when full it retains common backend execution credit while output waits. Queue input bytes and retained reply working bytes are different resources.",
    "wire": "Current grpc1.83.2 controlbuf.go preprocessData returns without data.Free for late DATA after stream removal; loopy run exit does not close all stream readers. These are source-based candidates for orphan buffers needing GC, not yet experimentally proven."
  },
